            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Howard L. Bolter, petitioners argue that Section\u202f1367 is a constitutional and sensible response by Congress to the serious procedural problems that were facing the Federal courts prior to 1990."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Bolter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Bolter, in a situation involving two States, the statute of limitations would probably not be tolled unless the case fell within California's time period; the statute itself, however, provides tolling."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Rotenberg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Rotenberg, respondents argue that the statute is unconstitutional because Congress lacks the power to enact a sweeping expansion of statutes of limitations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether sovereign immunity is a peculiarity that requires a state to waive it before a suit can proceed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "A Justice asked whether Congress can entirely forbid a state from enacting a similar statute of limitations."
      }
    ],
